1
00:00:00,282 --> 00:00:03,090
I open MergeWitness and run the comparison.

2
00:00:03,773 --> 00:00:12,735
The browser starts fresh workers for four Git snapshots: the
base project, tenant pricing, a product cache, and their clean
combination.

3
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:16,547
The ordinary Node suite passed in every snapshot.

4
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:20,996
Here, the same new behavior rule is checked across all four.

5
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:22,583
Base passes.

6
00:00:23,226 --> 00:00:24,427
Pricing alone passes.

7
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:26,105
Cache alone passes.

8
00:00:26,801 --> 00:00:28,609
The combined version fails.

9
00:00:29,291 --> 00:00:31,907
That is the interaction a green test suite missed.

10
00:00:32,827 --> 00:00:34,908
Now I inspect the exact sequence.

11
00:00:35,792 --> 00:00:38,828
Alpha requests a notebook and receives its ninety-dollar price.

12
00:00:39,558 --> 00:00:41,945
The cache stores that price under the notebook SKU.

13
00:00:42,972 --> 00:00:45,058
Beta requests the same notebook next.

14
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:49,517
Beta should pay one hundred dollars, but receives Alpha's
ninety-dollar value.

15
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:56,601
This is a concrete customer-boundary failure, with expected and
observed results that a maintainer can reproduce.

16
00:00:57,583 --> 00:01:00,944
IBM Bob helped turn the suspicion into executable evidence.

17
00:01:01,845 --> 00:01:06,959
In the first real IDE task, Bob authored an original interaction
probe and feature checks.

18
00:01:07,715 --> 00:01:10,082
You can open its task summary from this evidence tab.

19
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:15,578
Independent review then strengthened the frozen probe and cache
check before final verification.

20
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:22,727
The report records exactly which versions and hashes were
executed; the audit additions are not attributed to Bob.

21
00:01:23,649 --> 00:01:25,075
Next I open the repair tab.

22
00:01:25,734 --> 00:01:27,901
Bob authored a focused change to the catalog.

23
00:01:28,557 --> 00:01:33,825
Instead of one cache entry per product, it uses nested maps:
first by tenant, then by SKU.

24
00:01:34,813 --> 00:01:39,148
Human review caught a collision risk in an earlier flat key, and
Bob revised the candidate.

25
00:01:39,910 --> 00:01:41,581
I click Run verified candidate.

26
00:01:42,284 --> 00:01:49,836
A fresh browser worker now shows that Alpha still pays ninety,
Beta receives a fresh one hundred, and repeated requests still
benefit from caching.

27
00:01:51,033 --> 00:01:53,791
The repository also contains a second synthetic case.

28
00:01:54,319 --> 00:01:57,498
Bob wrote a priority-and-cursor probe plus two feature checks.

29
00:01:58,144 --> 00:02:02,981
Its clean combination skips an item even though the individual
changes and ordinary tests pass.

30
00:02:03,694 --> 00:02:07,252
We report that witness honestly; no repair is claimed for this
second case.

31
00:02:08,195 --> 00:02:15,626
Finally, the public repository holds all three real Bob task
summaries, the frozen checks, exact commits, and machine-
readable reports.

32
00:02:16,278 --> 00:02:20,347
MergeWitness gives a release reviewer a specific failing
sequence and a tested repair.

33
00:02:21,185 --> 00:02:26,240
A passing probe only describes that execution; it cannot certify
every possible merge.
